IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s01-06-definition`
IMPORT `theft-s07-14-offences`
IMPORT `theft-s15-21-fraud`
IMPORT `theft-s22-25-goods`
IMPORT `theft-s26-29-procedure`
IMPORT `theft-s30-36-general`
IMPORT `theft-schedules`

-- Theft Act 1968 (1968 c. 60) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who may be accused of an offence under the Theft Act 1968,
-- asking what the Act makes of what they did, or are said to have done, and the
-- most that can follow. There is no seat for the police, the prosecutor, a court
-- or any other official.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1968-60.txt, a plain-text rendering (not the official text)
-- of the legislation.gov.uk revised version of 2013-05-28.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules in the theft-*.l4 modules as the questions that
-- person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each
-- question builds the records those rules expect from plain inputs (yes or no,
-- numbers, dates and the modules' own choices), one input for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as they would be asked, and then
-- calls the same module rule.
--
-- A record field that the rules called never read is given a fixed placeholder
-- with a comment saying so.
--
-- Words of state of mind or judgment ("dishonestly", "reasonably", "believed")
-- are asked as the person's own answer. The questions never decide a question of
-- fact for the person, and nothing here predicts what a court would find.
--
-- Penalties are the greatest penalty the section itself states, as the section
-- states it (for example "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years"). The
-- Act gives fines as a LEVEL on the standard scale and does not state the sum for
-- a level; no sum is supplied here.
§§ `Section 1 -- theft`

-- s 1. Theft is dishonestly appropriating property belonging to another with the
-- intention of permanently depriving the other of it. Each of the five elements
-- is defined in ss 2 to 6; the questions in those sections below ask the
-- elements one at a time. By s 30(1) it makes no difference to the answer that the
-- owner is the accused's wife, husband or civil partner (theft-cases-s30-36.l4 asserts that).
@export Am I guilty of theft (s 1)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you dishonestly appropriated property belonging to another, intending permanently to deprive the other of it.
GIVEN `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had in law the right to deprive the other person of it, for yourself or for someone else?
      `I believed the other would have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe you would have the other person's consent if they had known of what you did and the circumstances of it?
      `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the person the property belongs to could not be found by taking reasonable steps?
      `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the property come to you as a trustee or as a personal representative?
      `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Leaving aside the beliefs asked above, was what you did dishonest by the standards of ordinary decent people? (The Act gives no test of dishonesty beyond those beliefs, so you state this yourself.)
      `I assumed the rights of an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you treat the property as an owner would, for example by using it, keeping it, selling it or giving it away?
      `I came by the property without stealing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you come by the property (innocently or not) without stealing it?
      `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you came by it, did you later assume a right to it by keeping it or dealing with it as owner?
      `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property, or a right or interest in it, transferred to you for value, or did it purport to be?
      `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you acting in good faith when it was transferred to you?
      `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights you later assumed rights that you believed you were acquiring?
      `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason anyone could call it theft a defect in the title of the person who transferred it to you?
      `what kind of thing it was` IS A `Kind of thing` @desc What kind of thing was it? Choose the closest description.
      `I was in possession of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land it was on or part of?
      `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a trustee, a personal representative, an attorney under a power of attorney, a company liquidator or otherwise authorised to sell or dispose of land belonging to another?
      `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deal with it in breach of the confidence placed in you?
      `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appropriate it by severing it from the land, by causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed?
      `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land under a tenancy (a tenancy for years or any shorter period, including an agreement for one)?
      `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay in possession after the tenancy ended, as a statutory tenant or otherwise?
      `it was a fixture or structure let with the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you took the whole or part of a fixture or structure that was let to be used with the land?
      `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pick it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose?
      `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person, and has possession not since been lost or abandoned?
      `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another person in the course of reducing it into possession?
      `another person had possession or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have possession or control of it?
      `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a proprietary right or interest in it?
      `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every such interest of another an equitable interest that arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest?
      `it was subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property subject to a trust?
      `another person had a right to enforce the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a right to enforce the trust?
      `I received it from or on account of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the property from, or on account of, another person?
      `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to that person to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way?
      `I got it through another person's mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get the property through another person's mistake?
      `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of the property, its proceeds or its value?
      `it is property of a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property that of a corporation sole (a single office-holder that is itself a legal person), whether or not the office is vacant?
      `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean the other person permanently to lose the thing itself?
      `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to treat the thing as your own to dispose of, regardless of the other person's rights?
      `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the way you meant to treat it a borrowing or a lending?
      `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the borrowing or lending for such a period, and in such circumstances, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal?
      `I had possession or control of the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have possession or control of the property, lawfully or not?
      `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with the property under a condition about getting it back that you might not be able to perform?
      `I parted with it for my own purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it for purposes of your own?
      `I parted with it without the other's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it without the other person's authority?
      `I meant to defeat the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to defeat the trust?
      `I meant not to make restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean not to make restoration?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of theft` IS
    `s 1 guilty of theft` `my theft facts`
    WHERE
        `my theft facts` MEANS `Theft facts` WITH
            `the dishonesty` IS `the dishonesty of my theft facts`
            `the appropriation` IS `the appropriation of my theft facts`
            `the thing taken` IS `the thing taken of my theft facts`
            `the belonging` IS `the belonging of my theft facts`
            `the intention` IS `the intention of my theft facts`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `with a view to gain or for his own benefit` IS FALSE
        `the dishonesty of my theft facts` MEANS `Dishonesty facts` WITH
            `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it`
            `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS `I believed the other would have consented`
            `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps`
            `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `willing to pay for the property` IS FALSE
            `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest`
        `the appropriation of my theft facts` MEANS `Appropriation facts` WITH
            `assumed the rights of an owner` IS `I assumed the rights of an owner`
            `came by the property without stealing it` IS `I came by the property without stealing it`
            `later assumed a right to it by keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner`
            `property or an interest in it was transferred, or purported to be, to him for value` IS `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value`
            `acted in good faith when it was transferred to him` IS `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me`
            `the rights assumed are rights he believed himself to be acquiring` IS `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring`
            `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the transferor's title` IS `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title`
        `the thing taken of my theft facts` MEANS `Thing taken` WITH
            `kind of thing` IS `what kind of thing it was`
            `in possession of the land` IS `I was in possession of the land`
            `authorised as trustee, personal representative, attorney or otherwise to sell or dispose of land belonging to another` IS `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land`
            `dealt with it in breach of the confidence reposed in him` IS `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me`
            `appropriated it by severing it, causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed` IS `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed`
            `in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy`
            `remains in possession of the land after a tenancy ended, as statutory tenant or otherwise` IS `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended`
            `it is a fixture or structure let to be used with the land` IS `it was a fixture or structure let with the land`
            `picked it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose` IS `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose`
            `it has been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person and possession has not since been lost or abandoned` IS `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it`
            `another person is in course of reducing it into possession` IS `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession`
        `the belonging of my theft facts` MEANS `Belonging facts` WITH
            `another had possession or control of it` IS `another person had possession or control of it`
            `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it`
            `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it`
            `it was subject to a trust` IS `it was subject to a trust`
            `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS `another person had a right to enforce the trust`
            `he received it from or on account of another` IS `I received it from or on account of another`
            `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way`
            `he got it by another's mistake` IS `I got it through another person's mistake`
            `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value`
            `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS `it is property of a corporation sole`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS FALSE
        `the intention of my theft facts` MEANS `Intention facts` WITH
            `meant the other permanently to lose the thing itself` IS `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently`
            `meant to treat the thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights`
            `the way he meant to treat it was a borrowing or lending` IS `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it`
            `the borrowing or lending was for a period and in circumstances making it equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal`
            `had possession or control of the property, lawfully or not` IS `I had possession or control of the property`
            `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet`
            `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS `I parted with it for my own purposes`
            `parted with it without the other's authority` IS `I parted with it without the other's authority`
            `meant to defeat the trust` IS `I meant to defeat the trust`
            `meant not to make restoration` IS `I meant not to make restoration`


§§ `Section 2 -- "dishonestly"`

-- s 2. The Act does not define dishonesty. It says three beliefs mean an appropriation is
-- not to be regarded as dishonest (a right in law to deprive the other, the other's consent,
-- and, except for a trustee or personal representative, that the owner cannot be found by
-- taking reasonable steps), and that an appropriation may be dishonest although the person
-- is willing to pay. Everything else is yours to state.
@export Was what I did dishonest (s 2)?
@desc Whether the appropriation is dishonest on the facts you state, taking into account the beliefs section 2(1) lists.
GIVEN `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had in law the right to deprive the other person of it, for yourself or for someone else?
      `I believed the other would have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe you would have the other person's consent if they had known of what you did and the circumstances of it?
      `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the person the property belongs to could not be found by taking reasonable steps?
      `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the property come to you as a trustee or as a personal representative?
      `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Leaving aside the beliefs asked above, was what you did dishonest by the standards of ordinary decent people? (The Act gives no test of dishonesty beyond those beliefs, so you state this yourself.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was what I did dishonest` IS
    `s 2 the appropriation is dishonest` `my dishonesty facts`
    WHERE
        `my dishonesty facts` MEANS `Dishonesty facts` WITH
            `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it`
            `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS `I believed the other would have consented`
            `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps`
            `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `willing to pay for the property` IS FALSE
            `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest`

§§ `Section 3 -- "appropriates"`

-- s 3. Any assumption by a person of the rights of an owner is an appropriation, including
-- later keeping or dealing with it as owner after coming by it without stealing it. A person
-- who buys in good faith for value does not commit theft only because the seller's title was
-- defective.
@export Did I appropriate the property (s 3)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you appropriated the property within section 3 in a way that can amount to theft.
GIVEN `I assumed the rights of an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you treat the property as an owner would, for example by using it, keeping it, selling it or giving it away?
      `I came by the property without stealing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you come by the property (innocently or not) without stealing it?
      `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you came by it, did you later assume a right to it by keeping it or dealing with it as owner?
      `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property, or a right or interest in it, transferred to you for value, or did it purport to be?
      `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you acting in good faith when it was transferred to you?
      `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights you later assumed rights that you believed you were acquiring?
      `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason anyone could call it theft a defect in the title of the person who transferred it to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I appropriate the property` IS
    `s 3 he appropriates, and the appropriation can amount to theft` `my appropriation facts`
    WHERE
        `my appropriation facts` MEANS `Appropriation facts` WITH
            `assumed the rights of an owner` IS `I assumed the rights of an owner`
            `came by the property without stealing it` IS `I came by the property without stealing it`
            `later assumed a right to it by keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner`
            `property or an interest in it was transferred, or purported to be, to him for value` IS `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value`
            `acted in good faith when it was transferred to him` IS `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me`
            `the rights assumed are rights he believed himself to be acquiring` IS `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring`
            `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the transferor's title` IS `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title`

§§ `Section 4 -- "property"`

-- s 4. Property includes money and all other property, real or personal, including things in
-- action and other intangible property. Land, things forming part of land, wild plants and wild
-- creatures can be stolen only in the cases s 4(2) to (4) set out.
@export Is the thing property that can be stolen (s 4)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, what you took is property that can be stolen within section 4.
GIVEN `what kind of thing it was` IS A `Kind of thing` @desc What kind of thing was it? Choose the closest description.
      `I was in possession of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land it was on or part of?
      `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a trustee, a personal representative, an attorney under a power of attorney, a company liquidator or otherwise authorised to sell or dispose of land belonging to another?
      `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deal with it in breach of the confidence placed in you?
      `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appropriate it by severing it from the land, by causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed?
      `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land under a tenancy (a tenancy for years or any shorter period, including an agreement for one)?
      `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay in possession after the tenancy ended, as a statutory tenant or otherwise?
      `it was a fixture or structure let with the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you took the whole or part of a fixture or structure that was let to be used with the land?
      `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pick it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose?
      `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person, and has possession not since been lost or abandoned?
      `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another person in the course of reducing it into possession?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the thing property that can be stolen` IS
    `s 4 the thing is property that can be stolen` `the thing I took`
    WHERE
        `the thing I took` MEANS `Thing taken` WITH
            `kind of thing` IS `what kind of thing it was`
            `in possession of the land` IS `I was in possession of the land`
            `authorised as trustee, personal representative, attorney or otherwise to sell or dispose of land belonging to another` IS `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land`
            `dealt with it in breach of the confidence reposed in him` IS `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me`
            `appropriated it by severing it, causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed` IS `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed`
            `in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy`
            `remains in possession of the land after a tenancy ended, as statutory tenant or otherwise` IS `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended`
            `it is a fixture or structure let to be used with the land` IS `it was a fixture or structure let with the land`
            `picked it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose` IS `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose`
            `it has been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person and possession has not since been lost or abandoned` IS `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it`
            `another person is in course of reducing it into possession` IS `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession`

§§ `Section 5 -- "belonging to another"`

-- s 5. Property belongs to anyone having possession or control of it, or any proprietary right
-- or interest in it (not an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or
-- grant one). Trusts, property received on account of another, property got by another's
-- mistake and a corporation sole's property are dealt with in s 5(2) to (5). The questions
-- about the wife, husband or civil partner of the owner (s 30(1)) change no answer here.
@export Does the property belong to another (s 5)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the property belongs to another person within section 5.
GIVEN `another person had possession or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have possession or control of it?
      `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a proprietary right or interest in it?
      `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every such interest of another an equitable interest that arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest?
      `it was subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property subject to a trust?
      `another person had a right to enforce the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a right to enforce the trust?
      `I received it from or on account of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the property from, or on account of, another person?
      `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to that person to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way?
      `I got it through another person's mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get the property through another person's mistake?
      `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of the property, its proceeds or its value?
      `it is property of a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property that of a corporation sole (a single office-holder that is itself a legal person), whether or not the office is vacant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the property belong to another` IS
    `s 5 the property belongs to another` `the belonging facts`
    WHERE
        `the belonging facts` MEANS `Belonging facts` WITH
            `another had possession or control of it` IS `another person had possession or control of it`
            `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it`
            `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it`
            `it was subject to a trust` IS `it was subject to a trust`
            `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS `another person had a right to enforce the trust`
            `he received it from or on account of another` IS `I received it from or on account of another`
            `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way`
            `he got it by another's mistake` IS `I got it through another person's mistake`
            `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value`
            `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS `it is property of a corporation sole`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS FALSE

§§ `Section 6 -- "with the intention of permanently depriving the other of it"`

-- s 6. A person is to be regarded as having that intention if the intention is to treat the
-- thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights; a borrowing or lending can
-- count if it is for a period and in circumstances equivalent to an outright taking, and so can
-- parting with it under a condition as to its return that he may not be able to perform. Ss 5(2)
-- and 5(4) add two more intentions that are regarded the same way.
@export Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it (s 6)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you intended permanently to deprive the other of the thing, as section 6 and sections 5(2) and 5(4) define that.
GIVEN `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean the other person permanently to lose the thing itself?
      `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to treat the thing as your own to dispose of, regardless of the other person's rights?
      `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the way you meant to treat it a borrowing or a lending?
      `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the borrowing or lending for such a period, and in such circumstances, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal?
      `I had possession or control of the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have possession or control of the property, lawfully or not?
      `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with the property under a condition about getting it back that you might not be able to perform?
      `I parted with it for my own purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it for purposes of your own?
      `I parted with it without the other's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it without the other person's authority?
      `I meant to defeat the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to defeat the trust?
      `I meant not to make restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean not to make restoration?
      `it was subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property subject to a trust?
      `another person had a right to enforce the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a right to enforce the trust?
      `I got it through another person's mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get the property through another person's mistake?
      `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of the property, its proceeds or its value?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` IS
    `s 6 he intends permanently to deprive the other of it` `my intention facts` `the belonging facts`
    WHERE
        `my intention facts` MEANS `Intention facts` WITH
            `meant the other permanently to lose the thing itself` IS `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently`
            `meant to treat the thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights`
            `the way he meant to treat it was a borrowing or lending` IS `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it`
            `the borrowing or lending was for a period and in circumstances making it equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal`
            `had possession or control of the property, lawfully or not` IS `I had possession or control of the property`
            `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet`
            `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS `I parted with it for my own purposes`
            `parted with it without the other's authority` IS `I parted with it without the other's authority`
            `meant to defeat the trust` IS `I meant to defeat the trust`
            `meant not to make restoration` IS `I meant not to make restoration`
        `the belonging facts` MEANS `Belonging facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `another had possession or control of it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS FALSE
            `it was subject to a trust` IS `it was subject to a trust`
            `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS `another person had a right to enforce the trust`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he received it from or on account of another` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS FALSE
            `he got it by another's mistake` IS `I got it through another person's mistake`
            `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS FALSE

§§ `Section 7 -- the penalty for theft`

-- s 7. A person guilty of theft is liable on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding seven years.
@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of theft (s 7)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had in law the right to deprive the other person of it, for yourself or for someone else?
      `I believed the other would have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe you would have the other person's consent if they had known of what you did and the circumstances of it?
      `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the person the property belongs to could not be found by taking reasonable steps?
      `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the property come to you as a trustee or as a personal representative?
      `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Leaving aside the beliefs asked above, was what you did dishonest by the standards of ordinary decent people? (The Act gives no test of dishonesty beyond those beliefs, so you state this yourself.)
      `I assumed the rights of an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you treat the property as an owner would, for example by using it, keeping it, selling it or giving it away?
      `I came by the property without stealing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you come by the property (innocently or not) without stealing it?
      `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you came by it, did you later assume a right to it by keeping it or dealing with it as owner?
      `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property, or a right or interest in it, transferred to you for value, or did it purport to be?
      `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you acting in good faith when it was transferred to you?
      `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights you later assumed rights that you believed you were acquiring?
      `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason anyone could call it theft a defect in the title of the person who transferred it to you?
      `what kind of thing it was` IS A `Kind of thing` @desc What kind of thing was it? Choose the closest description.
      `I was in possession of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land it was on or part of?
      `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a trustee, a personal representative, an attorney under a power of attorney, a company liquidator or otherwise authorised to sell or dispose of land belonging to another?
      `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deal with it in breach of the confidence placed in you?
      `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appropriate it by severing it from the land, by causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed?
      `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in possession of the land under a tenancy (a tenancy for years or any shorter period, including an agreement for one)?
      `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay in possession after the tenancy ended, as a statutory tenant or otherwise?
      `it was a fixture or structure let with the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you took the whole or part of a fixture or structure that was let to be used with the land?
      `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pick it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose?
      `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person, and has possession not since been lost or abandoned?
      `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another person in the course of reducing it into possession?
      `another person had possession or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have possession or control of it?
      `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a proprietary right or interest in it?
      `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every such interest of another an equitable interest that arises only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest?
      `it was subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property subject to a trust?
      `another person had a right to enforce the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another person have a right to enforce the trust?
      `I received it from or on account of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the property from, or on account of, another person?
      `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to that person to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way?
      `I got it through another person's mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get the property through another person's mistake?
      `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of the property, its proceeds or its value?
      `it is property of a corporation sole` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property that of a corporation sole (a single office-holder that is itself a legal person), whether or not the office is vacant?
      `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean the other person permanently to lose the thing itself?
      `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to treat the thing as your own to dispose of, regardless of the other person's rights?
      `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the way you meant to treat it a borrowing or a lending?
      `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the borrowing or lending for such a period, and in such circumstances, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal?
      `I had possession or control of the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have possession or control of the property, lawfully or not?
      `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with the property under a condition about getting it back that you might not be able to perform?
      `I parted with it for my own purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it for purposes of your own?
      `I parted with it without the other's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you part with it without the other person's authority?
      `I meant to defeat the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to defeat the trust?
      `I meant not to make restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean not to make restoration?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of theft` IS
    `s 7 liable on conviction on indictment for theft` `my theft facts`
    WHERE
        `my theft facts` MEANS `Theft facts` WITH
            `the dishonesty` IS `the dishonesty of my theft facts`
            `the appropriation` IS `the appropriation of my theft facts`
            `the thing taken` IS `the thing taken of my theft facts`
            `the belonging` IS `the belonging of my theft facts`
            `the intention` IS `the intention of my theft facts`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `with a view to gain or for his own benefit` IS FALSE
        `the dishonesty of my theft facts` MEANS `Dishonesty facts` WITH
            `believed in law he had the right to deprive the other of the property` IS `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it`
            `believed he would have the other's consent if the other knew` IS `I believed the other would have consented`
            `believed the owner cannot be discovered by taking reasonable steps` IS `I believed the owner could not be found by taking reasonable steps`
            `the property came to him as trustee or personal representative` IS `the property came to me as a trustee or personal representative`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `willing to pay for the property` IS FALSE
            `dishonest apart from the section 2(1) beliefs` IS `apart from those beliefs, what I did was dishonest`
        `the appropriation of my theft facts` MEANS `Appropriation facts` WITH
            `assumed the rights of an owner` IS `I assumed the rights of an owner`
            `came by the property without stealing it` IS `I came by the property without stealing it`
            `later assumed a right to it by keeping or dealing with it as owner` IS `I later started keeping or dealing with it as owner`
            `property or an interest in it was transferred, or purported to be, to him for value` IS `it was transferred, or purported to be transferred, to me for value`
            `acted in good faith when it was transferred to him` IS `I acted in good faith when it was transferred to me`
            `the rights assumed are rights he believed himself to be acquiring` IS `the rights I assumed are rights I believed I was acquiring`
            `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the transferor's title` IS `the only ground for calling it theft is a defect in the seller's title`
        `the thing taken of my theft facts` MEANS `Thing taken` WITH
            `kind of thing` IS `what kind of thing it was`
            `in possession of the land` IS `I was in possession of the land`
            `authorised as trustee, personal representative, attorney or otherwise to sell or dispose of land belonging to another` IS `I was authorised to sell or dispose of the land`
            `dealt with it in breach of the confidence reposed in him` IS `I dealt with it in breach of the confidence placed in me`
            `appropriated it by severing it, causing it to be severed, or after it had been severed` IS `I severed it, had it severed, or took it after it was severed`
            `in possession of the land under a tenancy` IS `I was in possession of the land under a tenancy`
            `remains in possession of the land after a tenancy ended, as statutory tenant or otherwise` IS `I stayed in possession after my tenancy ended`
            `it is a fixture or structure let to be used with the land` IS `it was a fixture or structure let with the land`
            `picked it for reward, or for sale or other commercial purpose` IS `I picked it for reward, for sale or for another commercial purpose`
            `it has been reduced into possession by or on behalf of another person and possession has not since been lost or abandoned` IS `another person had reduced it into possession and not lost or abandoned it`
            `another person is in course of reducing it into possession` IS `another person was in the course of reducing it into possession`
        `the belonging of my theft facts` MEANS `Belonging facts` WITH
            `another had possession or control of it` IS `another person had possession or control of it`
            `another had a proprietary right or interest in it` IS `another person had a proprietary right or interest in it`
            `every such interest of another is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant an interest` IS `every such interest is an equitable interest arising only from an agreement to transfer or grant it`
            `it was subject to a trust` IS `it was subject to a trust`
            `another had a right to enforce the trust` IS `another person had a right to enforce the trust`
            `he received it from or on account of another` IS `I received it from or on account of another`
            `he was under an obligation to that other to retain and deal with it or its proceeds in a particular way` IS `I was obliged to that person to keep it, or its proceeds, and deal with it in a particular way`
            `he got it by another's mistake` IS `I got it through another person's mistake`
            `he was under an obligation to make restoration, in whole or in part, of it, its proceeds or its value` IS `I was obliged to make restoration of it, its proceeds or its value`
            `it is property of a corporation sole, the office being vacant or not` IS `it is property of a corporation sole`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other is the wife or husband of the person who appropriates it` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the other's interest in it is derived from the marriage` IS FALSE
        `the intention of my theft facts` MEANS `Intention facts` WITH
            `meant the other permanently to lose the thing itself` IS `I meant the other to lose the thing itself permanently`
            `meant to treat the thing as his own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights` IS `I meant to treat it as my own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights`
            `the way he meant to treat it was a borrowing or lending` IS `what I meant to do was borrow or lend it`
            `the borrowing or lending was for a period and in circumstances making it equivalent to an outright taking or disposal` IS `the borrowing or lending was so long, or on such terms, that it was equivalent to an outright taking or disposal`
            `had possession or control of the property, lawfully or not` IS `I had possession or control of the property`
            `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet`
            `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS `I parted with it for my own purposes`
            `parted with it without the other's authority` IS `I parted with it without the other's authority`
            `meant to defeat the trust` IS `I meant to defeat the trust`
            `meant not to make restoration` IS `I meant not to make restoration`

§§ `Section 8 -- robbery`

-- s 8. A person is guilty of robbery if he steals, and immediately before or at the time of doing so,
-- and in order to do so, he uses force on any person or puts or seeks to put any person in fear of
-- being then and there subjected to force. An assault with intent to rob is punished the same way.
@export Am I guilty of robbery (s 8(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of robbery: theft done with the force or fear of force that section 8(1) describes.
GIVEN `I believed I had in law the right to deprive the other of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had in law the right to deprive the other person of it, for yourself or for someone else?
      `I believed the other would have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe you would have the other person's consent if they had known of what you did and the circumstances of it?
