            `parted with the property under a condition as to its return which he may not be able to perform` IS `I parted with it under a condition about its return that I might not be able to meet`
            `parted with it for purposes of his own` IS `I parted with it for my own purposes`
            `parted with it without the other's authority` IS `I parted with it without the other's authority`
            `meant to defeat the trust` IS `I meant to defeat the trust`
            `meant not to make restoration` IS `I meant not to make restoration`

§§ `Section 11 -- removal of articles from places open to the public`

-- s 11. Where the public have access to a building to view it, or a collection housed in it, a person who without
-- lawful authority removes from the building or its grounds the whole or part of an article displayed or kept for
-- display to the public there is guilty of an offence. It is no offence if he believes he has lawful authority or
-- would have it if the person entitled to give it knew. An article that is not part of, or on loan with, a
-- collection intended for permanent exhibition counts only if removed on a day the public have access.
@export Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public (s 11)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of removing an article from a building or its grounds that the public may visit.
GIVEN `the public have access to the building to view it or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the public have access to the building in order to view the building or part of it?
      `the public have access to view a collection housed in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the public have access in order to view a collection, or part of a collection, housed in the building?
      `the collection is made or shown in order to make sales or other commercial dealings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the collection made or exhibited for the purpose of effecting sales or other commercial dealings?
      `I removed the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds?
      `the article was displayed, or kept for display, to the public there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the article displayed, or kept for display, to the public in the building or that part of it or in its grounds?
      `I had lawful authority to remove it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove it with lawful authority?
      `the article was part of, or on loan with, a collection meant for permanent exhibition to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the article there as part of, or on loan for exhibition with, a collection intended for permanent exhibition to the public?
      `I removed it on a day when the public have access to the building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove it on a day when the public have access to the building?
      `I believed I had lawful authority for the removal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had lawful authority for the removal?
      `I believed I would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you would have had lawful authority if the person entitled to give it had known of the removal and the circumstances of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` IS
    `s 11 guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` `my removal facts`
    WHERE
        `my removal facts` MEANS `Removal facts` WITH
            `the public have access to the building in order to view it or part of it` IS `the public have access to the building to view it or part of it`
            `the public have access in order to view a collection or part of a collection housed in it` IS `the public have access to view a collection housed in it`
            `the collection is made or exhibited for the purpose of effecting sales or other commercial dealings` IS `the collection is made or shown in order to make sales or other commercial dealings`
            `removed from the building or its grounds the whole or part of an article` IS `I removed the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds`
            `the article was displayed or kept for display to the public in the building or that part of it or in its grounds` IS `the article was displayed, or kept for display, to the public there`
            `removed it with lawful authority` IS `I had lawful authority to remove it`
            `the article was there as part of, or on loan for exhibition with, a collection intended for permanent exhibition to the public` IS `the article was part of, or on loan with, a collection meant for permanent exhibition to the public`
            `removed it on a day when the public have access to the building` IS `I removed it on a day when the public have access to the building`
            `believed he had lawful authority for the removal` IS `I believed I had lawful authority for the removal`
            `believed he would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew of the removal and the circumstances` IS `I believed I would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of removing an article from a place open to the public (s 11(4))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `the public have access to the building to view it or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the public have access to the building in order to view the building or part of it?
      `the public have access to view a collection housed in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the public have access in order to view a collection, or part of a collection, housed in the building?
      `the collection is made or shown in order to make sales or other commercial dealings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the collection made or exhibited for the purpose of effecting sales or other commercial dealings?
      `I removed the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds?
      `the article was displayed, or kept for display, to the public there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the article displayed, or kept for display, to the public in the building or that part of it or in its grounds?
      `I had lawful authority to remove it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove it with lawful authority?
      `the article was part of, or on loan with, a collection meant for permanent exhibition to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the article there as part of, or on loan for exhibition with, a collection intended for permanent exhibition to the public?
      `I removed it on a day when the public have access to the building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remove it on a day when the public have access to the building?
      `I believed I had lawful authority for the removal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had lawful authority for the removal?
      `I believed I would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you would have had lawful authority if the person entitled to give it had known of the removal and the circumstances of it?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of removing an article from a place open to the public` IS
    `s 11(4) liable on conviction on indictment for removing an article` `my removal facts`
    WHERE
        `my removal facts` MEANS `Removal facts` WITH
            `the public have access to the building in order to view it or part of it` IS `the public have access to the building to view it or part of it`
            `the public have access in order to view a collection or part of a collection housed in it` IS `the public have access to view a collection housed in it`
            `the collection is made or exhibited for the purpose of effecting sales or other commercial dealings` IS `the collection is made or shown in order to make sales or other commercial dealings`
            `removed from the building or its grounds the whole or part of an article` IS `I removed the whole or part of an article from the building or its grounds`
            `the article was displayed or kept for display to the public in the building or that part of it or in its grounds` IS `the article was displayed, or kept for display, to the public there`
            `removed it with lawful authority` IS `I had lawful authority to remove it`
            `the article was there as part of, or on loan for exhibition with, a collection intended for permanent exhibition to the public` IS `the article was part of, or on loan with, a collection meant for permanent exhibition to the public`
            `removed it on a day when the public have access to the building` IS `I removed it on a day when the public have access to the building`
            `believed he had lawful authority for the removal` IS `I believed I had lawful authority for the removal`
            `believed he would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew of the removal and the circumstances` IS `I believed I would have lawful authority if the person entitled to give it knew`

§§ `Section 12 -- taking a conveyance without authority`

-- s 12. A person is guilty of an offence if, without the consent of the owner or other lawful authority,
-- he takes any conveyance for his own or another's use, or knowing it has been taken, drives it or allows
-- himself to be carried in or on it. He is not guilty if he did it believing he had lawful authority or
-- that the owner would have consented. Pedal cycles are dealt with in s 12(5).
@export Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority (s 12(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of taking a conveyance without the owner's consent or other lawful authority, or of driving or being carried in one you knew had been so taken.
GIVEN `it is built or adapted to carry a person or people by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a conveyance constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons, whether by land, water or air?
      `it is built or adapted for use only under the control of someone who is not carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it (for example a remote-controlled model)?
      `it is a pedal cycle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a pedal cycle?
      `it is the subject of a hiring or hire-purchase agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conveyance the subject of a hiring agreement or a hire-purchase agreement?
      `the owner consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the owner consent?
      `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is hired or on hire-purchase, did the person in possession under that agreement consent?
      `I had other lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have other lawful authority?
      `I took it for my own or another's use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take it for your own or another person's use?
      `I drove it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you drive it?
      `I allowed myself to be carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you allow yourself to be carried in or on it?
      `I knew it had been taken without such consent or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it had been taken without the owner's consent or other lawful authority?
      `I believed I had lawful authority to do what I did` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had lawful authority to do what you did?
      `I believed the owner would have consented if he knew` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you would have had the owner's consent if the owner had known of your doing it and the circumstances of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` IS
    `s 12(1) guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` `my conveyance facts`
    WHERE
        `my conveyance facts` MEANS `Conveyance facts` WITH
            `constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons by land, water or air` IS `it is built or adapted to carry a person or people by land, water or air`
            `constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it` IS `it is built or adapted for use only under the control of someone who is not carried in or on it`
            `it is a pedal cycle` IS `it is a pedal cycle`
            `it is the subject of a hiring agreement or hire-purchase agreement` IS `it is the subject of a hiring or hire-purchase agreement`
            `the owner consented` IS `the owner consented`
            `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented` IS `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented`
            `he had other lawful authority` IS `I had other lawful authority`
            `took it for his own or another's use` IS `I took it for my own or another's use`
            `drove it` IS `I drove it`
            `allowed himself to be carried in or on it` IS `I allowed myself to be carried in or on it`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `rode it` IS FALSE
            `knew it had been taken without such consent or authority` IS `I knew it had been taken without such consent or authority`
            `believed he had lawful authority to do what he did` IS `I believed I had lawful authority to do what I did`
            `believed he would have the owner's consent if the owner knew of his doing it and the circumstances` IS `I believed the owner would have consented if he knew`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of taking a conveyance without authority (s 12(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `it is built or adapted to carry a person or people by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a conveyance constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons, whether by land, water or air?
      `it is built or adapted for use only under the control of someone who is not carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it (for example a remote-controlled model)?
