§§ `Section 12A -- aggravated vehicle-taking`

-- s 12A. A person commits aggravated vehicle-taking if he commits the s 12(1) offence in relation to a
-- mechanically propelled vehicle and, after the taking and before it is recovered, it is driven dangerously on
-- a road or other public place, or an accident owing to the driving injures a person or damages property other than
-- the vehicle, or damage is caused to the vehicle. He is not guilty if he proves, for the proven driving, injury or
-- damage, that it occurred before he committed the basic offence or that he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate
-- vicinity of the vehicle when it occurred.
@export Am I guilty of aggravated taking of a vehicle (s 12A(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of aggravated vehicle-taking.
GIVEN `it is built or adapted to carry a person or people by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a conveyance constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons, whether by land, water or air?
      `it is built or adapted for use only under the control of someone who is not carried in or on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it (for example a remote-controlled model)?
