GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of aggravated taking of a vehicle` IS
    `s 12A(1) guilty of aggravated taking of a vehicle` `my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
    WHERE
        `my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Aggravated vehicle-taking facts` WITH
            `the basic offence` IS `the basic offence of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            `the vehicle he took is mechanically propelled` IS `the vehicle I took is mechanically propelled`
            `the dangerous driving` IS `the dangerous driving of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            `circumstance (a), driving dangerously` IS `circumstance (a), driving dangerously of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            `circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person` IS `circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            `circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle` IS `circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            `circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle` IS `circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the accident in circumstance (b) caused the death of the person concerned` IS FALSE
        `the basic offence of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Conveyance facts` WITH
            `constructed or adapted for the carriage of a person or persons by land, water or air` IS `it is built or adapted to carry a person or people by land, water or air`
            `constructed or adapted for use only under the control of a person not carried in or on it` IS `it is built or adapted for use only under the control of someone who is not carried in or on it`
            `it is a pedal cycle` IS `it is a pedal cycle`
            `it is the subject of a hiring agreement or hire-purchase agreement` IS `it is the subject of a hiring or hire-purchase agreement`
            `the owner consented` IS `the owner consented`
            `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented` IS `the person in possession under the hiring or hire-purchase agreement consented`
            `he had other lawful authority` IS `I had other lawful authority`
            `took it for his own or another's use` IS `I took it for my own or another's use`
            `drove it` IS `I drove it`
            `allowed himself to be carried in or on it` IS `I allowed myself to be carried in or on it`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `rode it` IS FALSE
            `knew it had been taken without such consent or authority` IS `I knew it had been taken without such consent or authority`
            `believed he had lawful authority to do what he did` IS `I believed I had lawful authority to do what I did`
            `believed he would have the owner's consent if the owner knew of his doing it and the circumstances` IS `I believed the owner would have consented if he knew`
        `the dangerous driving of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Dangerous driving facts` WITH
            `the vehicle was driven on a road or other public place` IS `it was driven on a road or other public place`
            `it was driven in a way which falls far below what would be expected of a competent and careful driver` IS `it was driven in a way that falls far below what a competent and careful driver would do`
            `it would be obvious to a competent and careful driver that driving in that way would be dangerous` IS `it would be obvious to a competent and careful driver that driving that way was dangerous`
        `circumstance (a), driving dangerously of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Vehicle-taking circumstance` WITH
            `the driving, accident or damage happened` IS `it happened, for circumstance (a), driving dangerously`
            `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken` IS `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken, for circumstance (a), driving dangerously`
            `by then the vehicle had been recovered, that is restored to its owner or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `by then the vehicle had been recovered, for circumstance (a), driving dangerously`
            `it happened before he committed the basic offence` IS `it happened before I committed the basic offence, for circumstance (a), driving dangerously`
            `he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate vicinity of the vehicle when it happened` IS `I was neither in nor on nor near the vehicle when it happened, for circumstance (a), driving dangerously`
        `circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Vehicle-taking circumstance` WITH
            `the driving, accident or damage happened` IS `it happened, for circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person`
            `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken` IS `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken, for circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person`
            `by then the vehicle had been recovered, that is restored to its owner or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `by then the vehicle had been recovered, for circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person`
            `it happened before he committed the basic offence` IS `it happened before I committed the basic offence, for circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person`
            `he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate vicinity of the vehicle when it happened` IS `I was neither in nor on nor near the vehicle when it happened, for circumstance (b), an accident owing to the driving injured a person`
        `circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Vehicle-taking circumstance` WITH
            `the driving, accident or damage happened` IS `it happened, for circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle`
            `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken` IS `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken, for circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle`
            `by then the vehicle had been recovered, that is restored to its owner or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `by then the vehicle had been recovered, for circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle`
            `it happened before he committed the basic offence` IS `it happened before I committed the basic offence, for circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle`
            `he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate vicinity of the vehicle when it happened` IS `I was neither in nor on nor near the vehicle when it happened, for circumstance (c), an accident owing to the driving damaged property other than the vehicle`
        `circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle of my aggravated vehicle-taking facts` MEANS `Vehicle-taking circumstance` WITH
            `the driving, accident or damage happened` IS `it happened, for circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle`
            `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken` IS `by then the vehicle had been unlawfully taken, for circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle`
            `by then the vehicle had been recovered, that is restored to its owner or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `by then the vehicle had been recovered, for circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle`
            `it happened before he committed the basic offence` IS `it happened before I committed the basic offence, for circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle`
            `he was neither in nor on nor in the immediate vicinity of the vehicle when it happened` IS `I was neither in nor on nor near the vehicle when it happened, for circumstance (d), damage was caused to the vehicle`

