§§ `Section 19 -- false statements by company directors`

-- s 19. Where an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association publishes or concurs in publishing a
-- written statement or account which to his knowledge is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material
-- particular, with intent to deceive members or creditors about its affairs, he is guilty of an offence.
@export Am I guilty of a false statement by an officer (s 19)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of publishing a false statement or account as an officer.
GIVEN `I am, or purport to be, an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or do you purport to act as one?
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members and I published as a member in my functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members, are you a member who published in connection with your functions of management?
      `I published, or agreed to the publishing of, a written statement or account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish, or concur in publishing, a written statement or account?
      `to my knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I intended to deceive its members about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive its members about its affairs?
      `I intended to deceive its creditors about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive its creditors about its affairs?
      `I intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for its benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of a false statement by an officer` IS
    `s 19 guilty of a false statement by an officer` `my statement facts`
    WHERE
        `my statement facts` MEANS `False statement facts` WITH
            `he is an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or purports to act as one` IS `I am, or purport to be, an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association`
            `the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members and he is a member publishing in connection with his functions of management` IS `the body's affairs are managed by its members and I published as a member in my functions of management`
            `published or concurred in publishing a written statement or account` IS `I published, or agreed to the publishing of, a written statement or account`
            `to his knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS `to my knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
            `he intended to deceive members about its affairs` IS `I intended to deceive its members about its affairs`
            `he intended to deceive creditors about its affairs` IS `I intended to deceive its creditors about its affairs`
            `he intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association` IS `I intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for its benefit`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of a false statement by an officer (s 19(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `I am, or purport to be, an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or do you purport to act as one?
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members and I published as a member in my functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members, are you a member who published in connection with your functions of management?
      `I published, or agreed to the publishing of, a written statement or account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish, or concur in publishing, a written statement or account?
      `to my knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular?
      `I intended to deceive its members about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive its members about its affairs?
      `I intended to deceive its creditors about its affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive its creditors about its affairs?
      `I intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for its benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of a false statement by an officer` IS
    `s 19(1) liable on conviction on indictment for a false statement by an officer` `my statement facts`
    WHERE
        `my statement facts` MEANS `False statement facts` WITH
            `he is an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association, or purports to act as one` IS `I am, or purport to be, an officer of a body corporate or unincorporated association`
            `the affairs of the body corporate or association are managed by its members and he is a member publishing in connection with his functions of management` IS `the body's affairs are managed by its members and I published as a member in my functions of management`
            `published or concurred in publishing a written statement or account` IS `I published, or agreed to the publishing of, a written statement or account`
            `to his knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS `to my knowledge the statement or account is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
            `he intended to deceive members about its affairs` IS `I intended to deceive its members about its affairs`
            `he intended to deceive creditors about its affairs` IS `I intended to deceive its creditors about its affairs`
            `he intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for the benefit of the body corporate or association` IS `I intended to deceive a person who has entered into a security for its benefit`

§§ `Section 20 -- suppression of documents`

-- s 20. A person who dishonestly, with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss to
-- another, destroys, defaces or conceals any valuable security, any will or other testamentary document, or any
-- original document of or belonging to or filed or deposited in a court of justice or any government department,
-- is guilty of an offence.
@export Am I guilty of suppressing a document (s 20(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of suppressing a valuable security, a will, or a court or government document.
GIVEN `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document create, transfer, surrender or release any right to, in or over property?
      `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document authorise the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right?
      `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the satisfaction of an obligation?
      `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a will or other testamentary document?
      `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice?
      `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, any government department?
      `I was dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing the document? (Section 2 does not define dishonesty here, so you state this yourself.)
      `I had in view a gain for myself or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have in view a gain for yourself or for another person? (A gain includes keeping what one already has.)
      `that gain was a gain in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the gain you had in view a gain in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I intended to cause loss to another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause loss to another person? (A loss includes not getting what one might get.)
      `that loss was a loss in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss you intended a loss in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I destroyed, defaced or concealed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you destroy, deface or conceal the document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of suppressing a document` IS
    `s 20(1) guilty of suppressing a document` `my suppression facts`
    WHERE
        `my suppression facts` MEANS `Suppression facts` WITH
            `the document` IS `the document of my suppression facts`
            `dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS `I was dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it`
            `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it of my suppression facts`
            `destroyed, defaced or concealed it` IS `I destroyed, defaced or concealed it`
        `the document of my suppression facts` MEANS `Document facts` WITH
            `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property`
            `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right`
            `it evidences the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the satisfaction of an obligation` IS `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation`
            `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS `it is a will or other testamentary document`
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice`
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department`
        `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it of my suppression facts` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
            `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS `I had in view a gain for myself or another`
            `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS `that gain was a gain in money or other property`
            `he intended to cause loss to another` IS `I intended to cause loss to another`
            `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS `that loss was a loss in money or other property`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of suppressing a document (s 20(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document create, transfer, surrender or release any right to, in or over property?
      `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document authorise the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right?
      `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the satisfaction of an obligation?
      `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a will or other testamentary document?
      `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice?
      `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, any government department?
      `I was dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing the document? (Section 2 does not define dishonesty here, so you state this yourself.)
      `I had in view a gain for myself or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have in view a gain for yourself or for another person? (A gain includes keeping what one already has.)
      `that gain was a gain in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the gain you had in view a gain in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I intended to cause loss to another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause loss to another person? (A loss includes not getting what one might get.)
      `that loss was a loss in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss you intended a loss in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I destroyed, defaced or concealed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you destroy, deface or conceal the document?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of suppressing a document` IS
    `s 20(1) liable on conviction on indictment for suppressing a document` `my suppression facts`
    WHERE
        `my suppression facts` MEANS `Suppression facts` WITH
            `the document` IS `the document of my suppression facts`
            `dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS `I was dishonest in destroying, defacing or concealing it`
            `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it` IS `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it of my suppression facts`
            `destroyed, defaced or concealed it` IS `I destroyed, defaced or concealed it`
        `the document of my suppression facts` MEANS `Document facts` WITH
            `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property`
            `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right`
            `it evidences the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the satisfaction of an obligation` IS `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation`
            `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS `it is a will or other testamentary document`
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice`
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department`
        `the gain or loss in view in destroying, defacing or concealing it of my suppression facts` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
            `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS `I had in view a gain for myself or another`
            `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS `that gain was a gain in money or other property`
            `he intended to cause loss to another` IS `I intended to cause loss to another`
            `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS `that loss was a loss in money or other property`

-- s 20(3). "Valuable security" means any document creating, transferring, surrendering or releasing any right to,
-- in or over property, or authorising the payment of money or delivery of any property, or evidencing the creation,
-- transfer, surrender or release of any such right, or the payment of money or delivery of any property, or the
-- satisfaction of any obligation.
@export Is the document a valuable security (s 20(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the document is a valuable security within section 20(3).
GIVEN `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document create, transfer, surrender or release any right to, in or over property?
      `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document authorise the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right?
      `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the payment of money or the delivery of property?
      `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document evidence the satisfaction of an obligation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the document a valuable security` IS
    `s 20(3) the document is a valuable security` `the document`
    WHERE
        `the document` MEANS `Document facts` WITH
            `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property` IS `it creates, transfers, surrenders or releases a right to, in or over property`
            `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it authorises the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right` IS `it is evidence of the creation, transfer, surrender or release of such a right`
            `it evidences the payment of money or the delivery of property` IS `it is evidence of the payment of money or the delivery of property`
            `it evidences the satisfaction of an obligation` IS `it is evidence of the satisfaction of an obligation`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is a will or other testamentary document` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a court of justice` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is an original document of or belonging to, or filed or deposited in, a government department` IS FALSE

§§ `Section 21 -- blackmail`

-- s 21. A person is guilty of blackmail if, with a view to gain for himself or another or with intent to cause loss
-- to another, he makes any unwarranted demand with menaces.
@export Am I guilty of blackmail (s 21(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of blackmail.
GIVEN `I had in view a gain for myself or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have in view a gain for yourself or for another person? (A gain includes keeping what one already has.)
      `that gain was a gain in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the gain you had in view a gain in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I intended to cause loss to another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause loss to another person? (A loss includes not getting what one might get.)
      `that loss was a loss in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss you intended a loss in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I made a demand with menaces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an unwarranted demand with menaces? (Section 21 explains what makes a demand unwarranted; it is answered by the questions that follow.)
      `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had reasonable grounds for making the demand?
      `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of blackmail` IS
    `s 21(1) guilty of blackmail` `my blackmail facts`
    WHERE
        `my blackmail facts` MEANS `Blackmail facts` WITH
            `the gain or loss in view in making the demand` IS `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts`
            `made a demand with menaces` IS `I made a demand with menaces`
            `he believed he had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand`
            `he believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the menaces relate to action to be taken by the person making the demand` IS FALSE
        `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
            `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS `I had in view a gain for myself or another`
            `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS `that gain was a gain in money or other property`
            `he intended to cause loss to another` IS `I intended to cause loss to another`
            `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS `that loss was a loss in money or other property`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of blackmail (s 21(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `I had in view a gain for myself or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have in view a gain for yourself or for another person? (A gain includes keeping what one already has.)
      `that gain was a gain in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the gain you had in view a gain in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I intended to cause loss to another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause loss to another person? (A loss includes not getting what one might get.)
      `that loss was a loss in money or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss you intended a loss in money or other property, temporary or permanent?
      `I made a demand with menaces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an unwarranted demand with menaces? (Section 21 explains what makes a demand unwarranted; it is answered by the questions that follow.)
      `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had reasonable grounds for making the demand?
      `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of blackmail` IS
    `s 21(3) liable on conviction on indictment for blackmail` `my blackmail facts`
    WHERE
        `my blackmail facts` MEANS `Blackmail facts` WITH
            `the gain or loss in view in making the demand` IS `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts`
            `made a demand with menaces` IS `I made a demand with menaces`
            `he believed he had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand`
            `he believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the menaces relate to action to be taken by the person making the demand` IS FALSE
        `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
            `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS `I had in view a gain for myself or another`
            `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS `that gain was a gain in money or other property`
            `he intended to cause loss to another` IS `I intended to cause loss to another`
            `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS `that loss was a loss in money or other property`

-- s 21(1). A demand with menaces is unwarranted unless the person making it does so in the belief that he has
-- reasonable grounds for making it, and that the use of the menaces is a proper means of reinforcing the demand.
-- The nature of the act or omission demanded is immaterial, and it is also immaterial whether the menaces relate
-- to action to be taken by the person making the demand.
@export Is my demand unwarranted (s 21(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the demand you made was unwarranted within section 21(1).
GIVEN `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that you had reasonable grounds for making the demand?
      `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my demand unwarranted` IS
    `s 21(1) the demand is unwarranted` `my blackmail facts`
    WHERE
        `my blackmail facts` MEANS `Blackmail facts` WITH
            `the gain or loss in view in making the demand` IS `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `made a demand with menaces` IS FALSE
            `he believed he had reasonable grounds for making the demand` IS `I believed I had reasonable grounds for making the demand`
            `he believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand` IS `I believed the use of the menaces was a proper means of reinforcing the demand`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the menaces relate to action to be taken by the person making the demand` IS FALSE
        `the gain or loss in view in making the demand of my blackmail facts` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he intended to cause loss to another` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE

§§ `Section 22 -- handling stolen goods`

-- s 22. A person handles stolen goods if (otherwise than in the course of the stealing), knowing or believing them
-- to be stolen goods, he dishonestly receives the goods, or dishonestly undertakes or assists in their retention,
-- removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another person, or if he arranges to do so.
@export Am I guilty of handling stolen goods (s 22(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of handling stolen goods.
GIVEN `where the goods came from` IS AN `Origin of goods` @desc Where did the goods come from? Choose the one that fits.
      `they are land, or a thing forming part of land not yet severed by stealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the goods land, or a thing forming part of land which has not been severed from it by stealing? (The Act says "goods" does not include land.)
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the stealing, or the blackmail, an offence under this Act?
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence where and when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it happened outside England and Wales, did the stealing or blackmail amount to an offence where and when it happened?
      `the fraud was an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the fraud amount to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006?
      `the money, or the part I am asked about, comes from the wrongful credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money (or the part of it you are asking about) derive from the wrongful credit?
      `they have been restored to the person they were stolen from, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the goods been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody?
      `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have that person and all claiming through them otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft?
      `it was done in the course of the stealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you did done in the course of the stealing?
      `I knew or believed the goods were stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know or believe the goods to be stolen goods?
      `I was dishonest in dealing with the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dishonest in dealing with the goods? (Section 2 does not define dishonesty here, so you state this yourself.)
      `I received the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the goods?
      `I undertook their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you undertake their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another person?
      `I assisted in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another person?
      `I arranged to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you arrange to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of handling stolen goods` IS
    `s 22(1) guilty of handling stolen goods` `my handling facts`
    WHERE
        `my handling facts` MEANS `Handling facts` WITH
            `the goods` IS `the goods of my handling facts`
            `it was done in the course of the stealing` IS `it was done in the course of the stealing`
            `he knew or believed the goods were stolen goods` IS `I knew or believed the goods were stolen goods`
            `dishonest in dealing with the goods` IS `I was dishonest in dealing with the goods`
            `he received the goods` IS `I received the goods`
            `he undertook the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of the goods by or for the benefit of another person` IS `I undertook their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another`
            `he assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of the goods by or for the benefit of another person` IS `I assisted in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another`
            `he arranged to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS `I arranged to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation`
        `the goods of my handling facts` MEANS `Goods facts` WITH
            `where the goods came from` IS `where the goods came from`
            `they are land, or a thing forming part of land that has not been severed from it by stealing` IS `they are land, or a thing forming part of land not yet severed by stealing`
            `the stealing, or the blackmail, was an offence under this Act` IS `the stealing or blackmail was an offence under this Act`
            `the stealing, or the blackmail, amounted to an offence where and when it happened` IS `the stealing or blackmail was an offence where and when it happened`
            `the fraud amounted to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS `the fraud was an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006`
            `the money, or the part of it asked about, derives from the wrongful credit` IS `the money, or the part I am asked about, comes from the wrongful credit`
            `they have been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `they have been restored to the person they were stolen from, or to other lawful possession or custody`
            `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft` IS `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution`

