GIVEN `where the goods came from` IS AN `Origin of goods` @desc Where did the goods come from? Choose the one that fits.
      `they are land, or a thing forming part of land not yet severed by stealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the goods land, or a thing forming part of land which has not been severed from it by stealing? (The Act says "goods" does not include land.)
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the stealing, or the blackmail, an offence under this Act?
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence where and when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it happened outside England and Wales, did the stealing or blackmail amount to an offence where and when it happened?
      `the fraud was an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the fraud amount to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006?
      `the money, or the part I am asked about, comes from the wrongful credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money (or the part of it you are asking about) derive from the wrongful credit?
      `they have been restored to the person they were stolen from, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the goods been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody?
      `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have that person and all claiming through them otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft?
      `it was done in the course of the stealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you did done in the course of the stealing?
      `I knew or believed the goods were stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know or believe the goods to be stolen goods?
      `I was dishonest in dealing with the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dishonest in dealing with the goods? (Section 2 does not define dishonesty here, so you state this yourself.)
      `I received the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the goods?
      `I undertook their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you undertake their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another person?
      `I assisted in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation by or for the benefit of another person?
      `I arranged to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you arrange to receive them, or to undertake or assist in their retention, removal, disposal or realisation?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of handling stolen goods` IS
    `s 22(2) liable on conviction on indictment for handling stolen goods` `my handling facts`
    WHERE
        `my handling facts` MEANS `Handling facts` WITH
            `the goods` IS `the goods of my handling facts`
            `it was done in the course of the stealing` IS `it was done in the course of the stealing`
            `he knew or believed the goods were stolen goods` IS `I knew or believed the goods were stolen goods`
            `dishonest in dealing with the goods` IS `I was dishonest in dealing with the goods`
            `he received the goods` IS `I received the goods`
