§§ `Section 23 -- advertising rewards for return of goods stolen or lost`

-- s 23. A person who publicly advertises a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost, and uses
-- words to the effect that no questions will be asked, that the person producing the goods will be safe from
-- apprehension or inquiry, or that money paid for them or lent on them will be repaid, is guilty of an offence;
-- so is the person who prints or publishes the advertisement.
@export Am I guilty of advertising a reward with no questions asked (s 23)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of advertising, printing or publishing a no-questions-asked reward notice.
GIVEN `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods stolen or lost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost?
      `it says, in effect, that no questions will be asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that no questions will be asked?
      `it says, in effect, that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry?
      `it says, in effect, that money paid for the goods or lent on them will be repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that money paid for the purchase of the goods, or advanced by way of loan on them, will be repaid?
      `I advertised the reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you advertise the reward?
      `I printed the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you print the advertisement?
      `I published the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish the advertisement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of advertising a reward with no questions asked` IS
    `s 23 guilty of advertising a reward with no questions asked` `my advertisement facts`
    WHERE
        `my advertisement facts` MEANS `Reward advertisement facts` WITH
            `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost` IS `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods stolen or lost`
            `it uses words to the effect that no questions will be asked` IS `it says, in effect, that no questions will be asked`
            `it uses words to the effect that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry` IS `it says, in effect, that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry`
            `it uses words to the effect that money paid for the purchase of the goods or advanced by way of loan on them will be repaid` IS `it says, in effect, that money paid for the goods or lent on them will be repaid`
            `he advertised the reward` IS `I advertised the reward`
            `he printed the advertisement` IS `I printed the advertisement`
            `he published the advertisement` IS `I published the advertisement`

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of advertising a reward with no questions asked (s 23)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods stolen or lost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost?
      `it says, in effect, that no questions will be asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that no questions will be asked?
      `it says, in effect, that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry?
      `it says, in effect, that money paid for the goods or lent on them will be repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it use words to the effect that money paid for the purchase of the goods, or advanced by way of loan on them, will be repaid?
      `I advertised the reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you advertise the reward?
      `I printed the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you print the advertisement?
      `I published the advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish the advertisement?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a charge`
DECIDE `What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of advertising a reward with no questions asked` IS
    `s 23 liable on summary conviction for advertising a reward with no questions asked` `my advertisement facts`
    WHERE
        `my advertisement facts` MEANS `Reward advertisement facts` WITH
            `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods which have been stolen or lost` IS `it is a public advertisement of a reward for the return of goods stolen or lost`
            `it uses words to the effect that no questions will be asked` IS `it says, in effect, that no questions will be asked`
            `it uses words to the effect that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry` IS `it says, in effect, that the person producing the goods will be safe from apprehension or inquiry`
            `it uses words to the effect that money paid for the purchase of the goods or advanced by way of loan on them will be repaid` IS `it says, in effect, that money paid for the goods or lent on them will be repaid`
            `he advertised the reward` IS `I advertised the reward`
            `he printed the advertisement` IS `I printed the advertisement`
            `he published the advertisement` IS `I published the advertisement`

§§ `Section 24 -- stolen goods`

-- s 24. Stolen goods are the goods originally stolen and parts of them, goods representing them in the hands of the
-- thief or a handler as the proceeds of disposal or realisation, goods obtained by blackmail or fraud in the cases
-- s 24(4) and (5) cover, and money dishonestly withdrawn from an account to which a wrongful credit was made. Goods
-- cease to be stolen goods once restored to the person from whom they were stolen or to lawful possession or custody,
-- or once he and all claiming through him have ceased to have any right to restitution (s 24(3)).
@export Are the goods stolen goods (s 24)?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the goods are stolen goods within section 24.
GIVEN `where the goods came from` IS AN `Origin of goods` @desc Where did the goods come from? Choose the one that fits.
      `they are land, or a thing forming part of land not yet severed by stealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the goods land, or a thing forming part of land which has not been severed from it by stealing? (The Act says "goods" does not include land.)
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the stealing, or the blackmail, an offence under this Act?
      `the stealing or blackmail was an offence where and when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it happened outside England and Wales, did the stealing or blackmail amount to an offence where and when it happened?
      `the fraud was an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the fraud amount to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006?
      `the money, or the part I am asked about, comes from the wrongful credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money (or the part of it you are asking about) derive from the wrongful credit?
      `they have been restored to the person they were stolen from, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the goods been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody?
      `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have that person and all claiming through them otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the goods stolen goods` IS
    `s 24 the goods are stolen goods` `the goods`
    WHERE
        `the goods` MEANS `Goods facts` WITH
            `where the goods came from` IS `where the goods came from`
            `they are land, or a thing forming part of land that has not been severed from it by stealing` IS `they are land, or a thing forming part of land not yet severed by stealing`
            `the stealing, or the blackmail, was an offence under this Act` IS `the stealing or blackmail was an offence under this Act`
            `the stealing, or the blackmail, amounted to an offence where and when it happened` IS `the stealing or blackmail was an offence where and when it happened`
            `the fraud amounted to an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS `the fraud was an offence under section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006`
            `the money, or the part of it asked about, derives from the wrongful credit` IS `the money, or the part I am asked about, comes from the wrongful credit`
            `they have been restored to the person from whom they were stolen, or to other lawful possession or custody` IS `they have been restored to the person they were stolen from, or to other lawful possession or custody`
            `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution in respect of the theft` IS `that person and anyone claiming through him have otherwise ceased to have any right to restitution`

§§ `Section 24A -- dishonestly retaining a wrongful credit`

-- s 24A. A person is guilty of an offence if a wrongful credit has been made to an account kept by him or in which
-- he has a right or interest, he knows or believes the credit is wrongful, and he dishonestly fails to take such steps
-- as are reasonable in the circumstances to secure that the credit is cancelled. A credit is wrongful to the extent that
-- it derives from theft, blackmail, fraud (contrary to s 1 of the Fraud Act 2006) or stolen goods.
@export Am I guilty of dishonestly retaining a wrongful credit (s 24A(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of dishonestly retaining a wrongful credit.
GIVEN `a credit of an amount of money has been made to an account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a credit of an amount of money been made to an account?
      `the account is kept by me, or I have a right or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account kept by you, or do you have a right or interest in it?
      `the account is kept with a bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account kept with a bank?
      `the account is kept with a business that lends out money received on deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account kept with a business in the course of which money received by way of deposit is lent to others?
      `the account is kept with a business another activity of which is financed out of deposits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account kept with a business another activity of which is financed wholly or to a material extent out of the capital of, or the interest on, money received by way of deposit?
      `the account is kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of the definition in regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `the credit comes at least in part from theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the credit derive, at least in part, from theft?
      `the credit comes at least in part from blackmail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the credit derive, at least in part, from blackmail?
      `the credit comes at least in part from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the credit derive, at least in part, from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006?
      `the credit comes at least in part from stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the credit derive, at least in part, from stolen goods?
      `I know or believe that the credit is wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know or believe that the credit is wrongful?
      `I did not take the steps that are reasonable in the circumstances to have the credit cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to secure that the credit is cancelled?
      `I was dishonest in failing to take those steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dishonest in failing to take those steps? (Section 2 does not define dishonesty here, so you state this yourself.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of dishonestly retaining a wrongful credit` IS
    `s 24A(1) guilty of dishonestly retaining a wrongful credit` `my credit facts`
    WHERE
        `my credit facts` MEANS `Wrongful credit facts` WITH
            `a credit of an amount of money has been made to an account` IS `a credit of an amount of money has been made to an account`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the credit is of money in a currency other than sterling` IS FALSE
            `the account is kept by him, or he has a right or interest in it` IS `the account is kept by me, or I have a right or interest in it`
            `the account is kept with a bank` IS `the account is kept with a bank`
            `the account is kept with a business in the course of which money received by way of deposit is lent to others` IS `the account is kept with a business that lends out money received on deposit`
            `the account is kept with a business another activity of which is financed wholly or to a material extent out of the capital of or the interest on money received by way of deposit` IS `the account is kept with a business another activity of which is financed out of deposits`
            `the account is kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of the definition in regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011` IS `the account is kept with an electronic money issuer within paragraphs (a) to (j) of regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the account was overdrawn before or after the credit was made` IS FALSE
            `the credit derives, at least in part, from theft` IS `the credit comes at least in part from theft`
            `the credit derives, at least in part, from blackmail` IS `the credit comes at least in part from blackmail`
            `the credit derives, at least in part, from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006` IS `the credit comes at least in part from fraud contrary to section 1 of the Fraud Act 2006`
            `the credit derives, at least in part, from stolen goods` IS `the credit comes at least in part from stolen goods`
            `he knows or believes that the credit is wrongful` IS `I know or believe that the credit is wrongful`
            `he failed to take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to secure that the credit is cancelled` IS `I did not take the steps that are reasonable in the circumstances to have the credit cancelled`
            `dishonest in failing to take those steps` IS `I was dishonest in failing to take those steps`

