§§ `Section 25 -- going equipped for stealing, etc.`

-- s 25. A person is guilty of an offence if, when not at his place of abode, he has with him any article for use in the
-- course of or in connection with any burglary or theft. By s 25(5) an offence under s 12(1) of taking a conveyance is
-- treated as theft for this purpose.
@export Am I guilty of going equipped (s 25(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you are guilty of going equipped for burglary, theft or taking a conveyance.
GIVEN `I was at my place of abode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you at your place of abode?
      `I had an article with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an article with you?
      `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary?
      `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft?
      `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority (an offence under section 12(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of going equipped` IS
    `s 25(1) guilty of going equipped` `my equipment facts`
    WHERE
        `my equipment facts` MEANS `Going equipped facts` WITH
            `he was at his place of abode` IS `I was at my place of abode`
            `he had an article with him` IS `I had an article with me`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority, an offence under section 12(1)` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft` IS FALSE

@export What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of going equipped (s 25(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the section makes what you did an offence and, if so, the most the section itself states can follow: how you are convicted, the longest imprisonment, and any fine level. The Act gives no sum for a fine level, and nothing here is a prediction of what a court would do.
GIVEN `I was at my place of abode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you at your place of abode?
