    `s 25(2) liable on conviction on indictment for going equipped` `my equipment facts`
    WHERE
        `my equipment facts` MEANS `Going equipped facts` WITH
            `he was at his place of abode` IS `I was at my place of abode`
            `he had an article with him` IS `I had an article with me`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft`
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority, an offence under section 12(1)` IS `I had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft` IS FALSE

-- s 25(3). Proof that he had with him an article made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft is evidence
-- that he had it with him for such use.
@export Is there evidence that I had the article for such use (s 25(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, section 25(3) makes the article's having been made or adapted evidence that you had it for use in a burglary or theft.
GIVEN `I had an article with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an article with you?
      `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the article made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there evidence that I had the article for such use` IS
    `s 25(3) there is evidence that he had the article for such use` `my equipment facts`
    WHERE
        `my equipment facts` MEANS `Going equipped facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he was at his place of abode` IS FALSE
            `he had an article with him` IS `I had an article with me`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a burglary` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with a theft` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he had it for use in the course of or in connection with taking a conveyance without authority, an offence under section 12(1)` IS FALSE
            `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft` IS `the article was made or adapted for use in committing a burglary or theft`

§§ `Section 26 -- search for stolen goods`

-- s 26(1). If it is made to appear to a justice of the peace, by information on oath, that there is reasonable cause to
-- believe that a person has in his custody or possession or on his premises any stolen goods, the justice may grant a
-- warrant to search the premises and seize the goods. The warrant is addressed to a constable, or to another person
-- only where an enactment expressly provides for that.
@export Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods (s 26(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, a justice may grant a warrant to search for and seize stolen goods.
GIVEN `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has information on oath been laid before a justice of the peace?
      `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that someone has stolen goods in his custody, possession or premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been made to appear to the justice that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in their custody or possession or on their premises? (Reasonable cause is the justice's judgment, so you state whether it has been made to appear.)
      `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the warrant addressed to a constable?
      `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the warrant addressed to someone other than a constable?
      `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an enactment expressly provide for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` IS
    `s 26(1) a justice may grant a warrant to search for and seize stolen goods` `the search facts`
    WHERE
        `the search facts` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
            `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace`
            `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that someone has stolen goods in his custody, possession or premises`
            `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS `the warrant is addressed to a constable`
            `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable`
            `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE

-- s 26(3). A person authorised by a warrant under this section to search premises for stolen goods may enter and search
-- the premises, and may seize any goods he believes to be stolen goods.
@export May the person with a warrant enter and search my premises (s 26(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the person searching may enter and search your premises under section 26(3).
GIVEN `the searcher is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person searching authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the person with a warrant enter and search my premises` IS
    `s 26(3) he may enter and search the premises` `the search facts`
    WHERE
        `the search facts` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
            `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS `the searcher is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS FALSE

@export May the person searching seize goods he believes to be stolen (s 26(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the person searching may seize goods he believes to be stolen goods.
GIVEN `the searcher is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person searching authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods?
      `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person searching believe the goods to be stolen goods?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the person searching seize goods he believes to be stolen` IS
    `s 26(3) he may seize any goods he believes to be stolen goods` `the search facts`
    WHERE
        `the search facts` MEANS `Search facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `information on oath has been laid before a justice of the peace` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it has been made to appear that there is reasonable cause to believe that a person has stolen goods in his custody or possession or on his premises` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the warrant is addressed to a constable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the warrant is addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `an enactment expressly provides for a warrant to be addressed to someone other than a constable` IS FALSE
            `he is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods` IS `the searcher is authorised under section 26 to search the premises for stolen goods`
            `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods` IS `the searcher believes the goods to be stolen goods`

§§ `Section 27 -- evidence and procedure on a charge of theft or handling stolen goods`

-- s 27(1). Persons charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft, at different times or at the same
-- time, may be indicted together and tried together, whether or not the person who stole them is also indicted.
@export May I be charged and tried together with others for handling goods from the same theft (s 27(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, you may be charged in one indictment with others and tried with them.
GIVEN `I am charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft?
      `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are others charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, whether at different times or at the same time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be charged and tried together with others for handling goods from the same theft` IS
    `s 27(1) he may be charged in one indictment with others and tried with them` `the joint facts`
    WHERE
        `the joint facts` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
            `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS `I am charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft`
            `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS FALSE

-- s 27(2). On the trial of two or more persons indicted for jointly handling stolen goods, the jury may find any of
-- them guilty if satisfied that he handled all or any of the goods, whether or not he did so jointly with the others.
@export May the jury find me guilty although I did not handle the goods jointly (s 27(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the jury may find you guilty whether or not you handled the goods jointly.
GIVEN `two or more of us are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are two or more persons, including you, indicted for jointly handling stolen goods?
      `the jury are satisfied that I handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the jury satisfied that you handled all or any of the stolen goods?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the jury find me guilty although I did not handle the goods jointly` IS
    `s 27(2) the jury may find him guilty whether or not he handled the goods jointly` `the joint facts`
    WHERE
        `the joint facts` MEANS `Joint handling facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he is charged with handling all or any of the stolen goods from a theft` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `others are charged in the same indictment with handling goods from the same theft, at different times or at the same time` IS FALSE
            `two or more persons are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods` IS `two or more of us are indicted for jointly handling stolen goods`
            `the jury are satisfied that he handled all or any of the stolen goods` IS `the jury are satisfied that I handled all or any of the stolen goods`

-- s 27(3). Where a person is being proceeded against for handling stolen goods (and for no other offence) and evidence
-- has been given of his having or arranging to have the goods in his possession, or of his undertaking or assisting in
-- their retention, removal, disposal or realisation, evidence may be given, for the purpose of proving that he knew or
-- believed the goods to be stolen, (a) that he has had in his possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention,
-- removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from any theft taking place not earlier than twelve months before
-- the offence charged, and (b) that he has within the five years preceding the date of the offence charged been
-- convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods, if seven days' notice in writing has been given to him of the
-- intention to prove the conviction.
@export May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen (s 27(3))?
@desc Whether, on the facts and dates you state, evidence of other dealings in stolen goods or of an earlier conviction is admissible to prove that you knew or believed the goods to be stolen.
GIVEN `I am being proceeded against for handling stolen goods and for no other offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being proceeded against for handling stolen goods, and for no other offence?
      `evidence has been given that I had, or arranged to have, the goods in my possession, or undertook or assisted in, or arranged to undertake or assist in, their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has evidence been given of your having, or arranging to have, the goods in your possession, or of your undertaking or assisting in, or arranging to undertake or assist in, their retention, removal, disposal or realisation?
      `the evidence is that I have had in my possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from another theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence offered that you have had in your possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from any other theft?
      `the day of that other theft` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that other theft take place?
      `the day of the offence charged` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence you are charged with committed?
      `the evidence is that I have been convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence offered that you have been convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods?
      `the day of that conviction` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted?
      `days of written notice I was given of the intention to prove the conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days' written notice were you given of the intention to prove the conviction? (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` IS
    `s 27(3) evidence is admissible to prove he knew or believed the goods to be stolen goods` `the evidence facts`
    WHERE
        `the evidence facts` MEANS `Previous dealings evidence facts` WITH
            `he is being proceeded against for handling stolen goods and for no other offence` IS `I am being proceeded against for handling stolen goods and for no other offence`
            `evidence has been given of his having, or arranging to have, the goods in his possession, or of his undertaking or assisting in, or arranging to undertake or assist in, their retention, removal, disposal or realisation` IS `evidence has been given that I had, or arranged to have, the goods in my possession, or undertook or assisted in, or arranged to undertake or assist in, their retention, removal, disposal or realisation`
            `the evidence is that he has had in his possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from another theft` IS `the evidence is that I have had in my possession, or undertaken or assisted in the retention, removal, disposal or realisation of, stolen goods from another theft`
            `the date of that other theft` IS `the day of that other theft`
            `the date of the offence charged` IS `the day of the offence charged`
            `the evidence is that he has been convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods` IS `the evidence is that I have been convicted of theft or of handling stolen goods`
            `the date of that conviction` IS `the day of that conviction`
            `days of written notice given to him of the intention to prove the conviction` IS `days of written notice I was given of the intention to prove the conviction`

-- s 27(4). In proceedings for the theft of anything in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a
-- theft, a statutory declaration by a person who despatched or received the goods or a postal packet, or by a person
-- who is in a position to say what state they were in, is admissible as evidence of the facts stated, if oral evidence to
-- the like effect would have been admissible, a copy was given to the person charged at least seven days before the
-- hearing or trial, and he did not give the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend at least three
-- days before it, or within such further time as the court allows.
@export Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states (s 27(4))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the statutory declaration is admissible as evidence of the facts stated.
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the theft of something in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a theft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for the theft of anything in the course of transmission (by post or otherwise), or for handling stolen goods from such a theft?
      `the declaration says that the declarant despatched, received or failed to receive goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state when despatched or received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the declaration say that the declarant despatched, or received, or failed to receive, goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state or condition when despatched or received?
      `oral evidence to the like effect would have been admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would oral evidence to the like effect have been admissible in the proceedings?
      `days before the hearing that a copy was given to the person charged` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the hearing or trial was a copy of the declaration given to the person charged?
      `the person charged gave the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person charged give the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend?
      `days before the hearing that the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the hearing or trial was that notice given? (0 if none)
      `the court allowed further time in special circumstances and the notice was given within it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court allow further time in special circumstances, and was the notice given within it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` IS
    `s 27(4) the statutory declaration is admissible as evidence of the facts stated` `the declaration facts`
    WHERE
        `the declaration facts` MEANS `Statutory declaration facts` WITH
            `the proceedings are for the theft of anything in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a theft` IS `the proceedings are for the theft of something in the course of transmission, or for handling stolen goods from such a theft`
            `the declaration says that the declarant despatched or received or failed to receive goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state or condition when despatched or received` IS `the declaration says that the declarant despatched, received or failed to receive goods or a postal packet, or that they were in a particular state when despatched or received`
            `oral evidence to the like effect would have been admissible in the proceedings` IS `oral evidence to the like effect would have been admissible`
            `days before the hearing or trial that a copy of the declaration was given to the person charged` IS `days before the hearing that a copy was given to the person charged`
            `the person charged gave the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend` IS `the person charged gave the prosecutor written notice requiring the declarant to attend`
            `days before the hearing or trial that he gave that notice` IS `days before the hearing that the notice was given`
            `the court allowed further time in special circumstances and he gave the notice within it` IS `the court allowed further time in special circumstances and the notice was given within it`

§§ `Section 29 -- summary trial`

-- s 29(2). An indictable offence under this Act is, with the other exceptions shown, an offence that paragraph 11 of Schedule 1 to
-- the Magistrates' Courts Act 1952 lists as triable summarily with the accused's consent. The paragraph excepts robbery,
-- aggravated burglary, blackmail and assault with intent to rob, certain burglaries, and handling goods from an offence
-- not committed in the United Kingdom. That Act is not among the inputs and was replaced, so this says only what the paragraph said.
@export Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent (s 29(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, paragraph 11 of Schedule 1 to the Magistrates' Courts Act 1952, as section 29(2) substituted it, lists your offence as triable summarily with your consent.
GIVEN `the offence is an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence you are charged with an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968?
      `it is robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob?
      `it is a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence not included in that Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence which is not included in the 1952 Schedule?
      `it is a burglary in a dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a burglary in a dwelling?
      `entry was obtained by force or deception or by the use of any tool, key or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was entry to the dwelling, or to the part of it where the burglary was committed, or to any building or part of a building containing the dwelling, obtained by force or deception, or by the use of any tool, key or appliance?
      `a person in the dwelling was subjected to violence or the threat of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any person in the dwelling subjected to violence or the threat of violence?
      `it is handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` IS
    `s 29(2) paragraph 11 lists the offence as one that may be tried summarily with his consent` `the trial facts`
    WHERE
        `the trial facts` MEANS `Summary trial facts` WITH
            `the offence is an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968` IS `the offence is an indictable offence under the Theft Act 1968`
            `it is robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob` IS `it is robbery, aggravated burglary, blackmail or assault with intent to rob`
            `it is a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence which is not included in that Schedule` IS `it is a burglary comprising the commission of, or an intention to commit, an offence not included in that Schedule`
            `it is a burglary in a dwelling` IS `it is a burglary in a dwelling`
            `entry to the dwelling, or to the part of it where the burglary was committed, or to any building or part of a building containing the dwelling, was obtained by force or deception or by the use of any tool, key or appliance` IS `entry was obtained by force or deception or by the use of any tool, key or appliance`
            `a person in the dwelling was subjected to violence or the threat of violence` IS `a person in the dwelling was subjected to violence or the threat of violence`
            `it is handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom` IS `it is handling stolen goods from an offence not committed in the United Kingdom`

§§ `Section 30 -- husband and wife, and civil partners`

-- s 30(2). Subject to s 30(4), a person has the same right to bring proceedings against his or her wife or husband for any
-- offence (whether under this Act or otherwise) as if they were not married, and a person bringing such proceedings is competent
-- to give evidence for the prosecution at every stage. So the accused's wife or husband may bring proceedings against the accused.
@export May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married (s 30(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, your wife or husband may bring proceedings against you as if you were not married, subject to section 30(4).
GIVEN `the step taken against me` IS A `Step against him` @desc What step is being taken against you?
      `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property that belonged to my wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to your wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence?
      `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the step taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions?
      `I am charged with committing the offence jointly with my wife, husband or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with committing the offence jointly with your wife, husband or civil partner?
      `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) my wife or husband and I were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By a judicial decree or order (wherever made), were you and your wife or husband at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit?
      `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of my civil partner and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an order (wherever made) in force providing for the separation of you and your civil partner?
      `the person bringing the proceedings is my wife or husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person bringing the proceedings your wife or husband?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married` IS
    `s 30(2) his wife or husband may bring proceedings against him as if they were not married` `the spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `the spouse facts` MEANS `Spouse proceedings facts` WITH
            `the step taken` IS `the step taken against me`
            `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to his wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence` IS `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property that belonged to my wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to do so`
            `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions`
            `he is charged with committing the offence jointly with his wife, husband or civil partner` IS `I am charged with committing the offence jointly with my wife, husband or civil partner`
            `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) he and his wife or husband were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) my wife or husband and I were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit`
            `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of him and his civil partner` IS `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of my civil partner and me`
            `the person bringing the proceedings is his wife or husband` IS `the person bringing the proceedings is my wife or husband`

@export Is my wife or husband a competent witness for the prosecution (s 30(2))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, the spouse who brought the proceedings is competent to give evidence for the prosecution.
GIVEN `the person bringing the proceedings is my wife or husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person bringing the proceedings your wife or husband?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my wife or husband a competent witness for the prosecution` IS
    `s 30(2) the spouse who brings the proceedings is competent to give evidence for the prosecution` `the spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `the spouse facts` MEANS `Spouse proceedings facts` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the step taken` IS `some other step`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to his wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `he is charged with committing the offence jointly with his wife, husband or civil partner` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) he and his wife or husband were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of him and his civil partner` IS FALSE
            `the person bringing the proceedings is his wife or husband` IS `the person bringing the proceedings is my wife or husband`

-- s 30(4). Proceedings against a person for stealing or doing unlawful damage to property belonging to his wife, husband or civil partner
-- (or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy) may not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Director of Public
-- Prosecutions, unless he is charged jointly with the spouse, or a judicial decree says there is no obligation to cohabit, or a
-- separation order is in force for a civil partner. By s 30(5) this extends to an arrest by the spouse and a warrant on the spouse's information.
@export May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property (s 30(4))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, section 30(4) allows the step to be taken against you without the Director of Public Prosecutions having consented.
GIVEN `the step taken against me` IS A `Step against him` @desc What step is being taken against you?
      `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property that belonged to my wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to your wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence?
      `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the step taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions?
      `I am charged with committing the offence jointly with my wife, husband or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with committing the offence jointly with your wife, husband or civil partner?
      `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) my wife or husband and I were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By a judicial decree or order (wherever made), were you and your wife or husband at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit?
      `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of my civil partner and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an order (wherever made) in force providing for the separation of you and your civil partner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` IS
    `s 30(4) the step may be taken` `the spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `the spouse facts` MEANS `Spouse proceedings facts` WITH
            `the step taken` IS `the step taken against me`
            `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property which at the time belonged to his wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to commit such an offence` IS `the offence is stealing, or doing unlawful damage to, property that belonged to my wife, husband or civil partner, or an attempt, incitement or conspiracy to do so`
            `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS `the step is taken by or with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions`
            `he is charged with committing the offence jointly with his wife, husband or civil partner` IS `I am charged with committing the offence jointly with my wife, husband or civil partner`
            `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) he and his wife or husband were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit` IS `by a judicial decree or order (wherever made) my wife or husband and I were at the time of the offence under no obligation to cohabit`
            `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of him and his civil partner` IS `an order (wherever made) is in force providing for the separation of my civil partner and me`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the person bringing the proceedings is his wife or husband` IS FALSE

§§ `Section 31 -- effect on civil proceedings and rights`

-- s 31(1). A person is not excused from answering a question put to him, or complying with an order made, in proceedings for the
-- recovery or administration of property, the execution of a trust or an account of property or dealings with property, on the
-- ground that it may incriminate him or his spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act.
@export Am I excused from answering because it may incriminate me or my spouse (s 31(1))?
@desc Whether, on the facts you state, section 31(1) removes that excuse, so that you must answer or comply.
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of property, the execution of a trust, or an account of property or dealings with property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property, for the execution of any trust, or for an account of any property or dealings with property?
      `I would be excused from the question or the order only because answering or complying may incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be excused from answering the question or complying with the order only because it may incriminate you, or your spouse or civil partner, of an offence under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from answering because it may incriminate me or my spouse` IS
    `s 31(1) he is not excused from answering the question or complying with the order` `the civil proceedings facts`
    WHERE
        `the civil proceedings facts` MEANS `Civil proceedings facts` WITH
            `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of any property, for the execution of any trust or for an account of any property or dealings with property` IS `the proceedings are for the recovery or administration of property, the execution of a trust, or an account of property or dealings with property`
            `he would be excused from the question or the order only because answering or complying may incriminate him or his spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act` IS `I would be excused from the question or the order only because answering or complying may incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner of an offence under this Act`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the statement or admission was made in answering a question put, or complying with an order made, in such proceedings` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is offered in proceedings for an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is offered against him` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `it is offered against his spouse or civil partner` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `they married or became civil partners after the statement or admission was made` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `property has been stolen or obtained by fraud or other wrongful means` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rules called never read this field.
            `the only thing said to affect the title is the conviction of the offender` IS FALSE

